error[E0277]: the trait bound `Raw<'a>: structio::beve::Read<'_>` is not satisfied
  --> tests/ui/raw_in_both_formats.rs:13:1
   |
13 | structio::object!(['a] Envelope<'a> { id, payload });
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   | |
   | the trait `structio::beve::Read<'_>` is not implemented for `Raw<'a>`
   | required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = note: a type becomes readable by being declared with `structio::object!` or `#[derive(Structio)]`, or by a `beve::Read` impl written by hand
   = note: a declaration generates both directions unless it narrows to one: a struct that is only ever written is declared `object!(write_only ..)` or `#[structio(write_only)]`, and then nothing in it needs a read impl
   = note: where the struct really is read, a stub whose body is `r.skip_value()` is legitimate there
   = note: `Raw<'a>` implements similarly named trait `structio::json::Read`, but not `structio::beve::Read<'_>`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `structio::beve::Read<'de>`:
             $IMPLEMENTORS
   = note: this error originates in the macro `$crate::__beve_read_impls` which comes from the expansion of the macro `structio::object` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

error[E0277]: the trait bound `Raw<'_>: structio::beve::Write` is not satisfied
  --> tests/ui/raw_in_both_formats.rs:13:1
   |
13 | structio::object!(['a] Envelope<'a> { id, payload });
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   | |
   | the trait `structio::beve::Write` is not implemented for `Raw<'_>`
   | required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = note: a type becomes writable by being declared with `structio::object!` or `#[derive(Structio)]`, or by a `beve::Write` impl written by hand
   = note: the direction axis narrows only to the write half -- there is no `read_only` -- so a type used in a struct that is only ever read still needs this impl
   = note: there is no empty stub: a member that writes nothing truncates the object. `w.write_null()` with `is_null` returning `true` lets `SkipNull` drop the member
   = note: `Raw<'_>` implements similarly named trait `structio::json::Write`, but not `structio::beve::Write`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `structio::beve::Write`:
             $IMPLEMENTORS
